---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import { MotionGestureReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-gesture.tsx';
import { MotionGestureAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-gesture.ts';
import MotionGestureSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-gesture.svelte';
import reactSource from '@/examples/react/motion-gesture.tsx?raw';
import angularSource from '@/examples/angular/motion-gesture.ts?raw';
import svelteSource from '@/examples/svelte/motion-gesture.svelte?raw';
import { demoClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage title="Motion: gestures" description="Pointer gestures on an element, drag, swipe and reorder, each with the keyboard alternative it must have.">
  <h1>Gestures</h1>
  <p>A gesture moves an element with the pointer, and gives it a keyboard alternative, so the page works without a pointer. Define it once, from <code>@udixio/motion/gesture</code>, and mark the element with <code>data-motion-gesture="&lt;name&gt;"</code>.</p>

  <h2>Define</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineGesture } from '@udixio/motion/gesture';

defineGesture('dismiss', { kind: 'swipe', alternative: 'action' });`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>drag</code> follows the pointer on <code>axis</code> <code>x</code>, <code>y</code> or <code>both</code> (the default). It stays within its parent (<code>bounds: 'parent'</code>, the default), or moves freely with <code>bounds: 'none'</code>. Released, it is thrown on by 0.2 s of its velocity, within its bounds, and glides there with the release spring. Its alternative is <code>arrows</code>: the arrow keys move it 16 px, or 64 px with Shift.</li>
    <li><code>swipe</code> follows the pointer on <code>axis</code> <code>x</code> (the default) or <code>y</code>. Released past 40 % of its size, or at more than 800 px/s in its direction, it flies out and fades; released sooner, it springs back. Its alternative is <code>action</code>: Delete or Backspace swipes the focused element towards the end.</li>
    <li><code>reorder</code> moves the element among its siblings that carry the same gesture, on <code>axis</code> <code>y</code> (the default) or <code>x</code>, past each neighbour its centre crosses. Its alternative is <code>grab</code>: Space or Enter grabs the focused element, the arrow keys of its axis move it, Space or Enter drops it, and Escape puts it back where it was.</li>
    <li><code>release</code> is the spring of the release: <code>spring.default.spatial</code> by default.</li>
    <li><code>alternative</code> is required and must be the one of its kind. It is what makes the gesture operable without a pointer (WCAG 2.1.1 and 2.5.7).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>HTML</h2>
  <pre><code>{`<div data-motion-gesture="dismiss">…</div>

import { connectMotion } from '@udixio/motion';
connectMotion(); // binds data-motion-gesture like data-motion`}</code></pre>
  <p>An element carries one gesture at a time. In JavaScript, <code>gesture(card, 'dismiss')</code> binds one to an element, <code>binding.offset</code> gives where it is held, <code>binding.reset()</code> sends it back with the release spring, and <code>destroy()</code> gives back what the gesture set on the element.</p>

  <h2>Events</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>motion-dragend</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; x, y &#125;</code>, when a released drag has come to rest. It cannot be prevented.</li>
    <li><code>motion-swipe</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; direction &#125;</code> (<code>'start'</code> or <code>'end'</code>), when a swipe is released far or fast enough, or Delete is pressed. It is cancelable: <code>preventDefault()</code> keeps the element where it is, and it springs back. Without it, the element flies out and is <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> once out of sight; removing it is the page's job.</li>
    <li><code>motion-reorder</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; from, to &#125;</code>, before each step of a reorder, by pointer or by keyboard. It is cancelable: <code>preventDefault()</code> refuses the step.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A reorder announces each keyboard step in a visually hidden live region with <code>role="status"</code>, for example <code>Moved. Position 3 of 5.</code></p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>Drag the chip with the pointer, and it keeps its momentum when released. Or focus it and use the arrow keys.</p>
  <div class={demoClass}>
    <div class="relative h-48 w-full rounded-3xl bg-surface-container">
      <button type="button" data-motion-gesture="gesture-html-drag" class="absolute left-4 top-4 cursor-grab rounded-full bg-primary px-5 py-3 text-label-large text-on-primary focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-on-surface">Drag me</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineGesture } from '@udixio/motion/gesture';
defineGesture('gesture-html-drag', { kind: 'drag', alternative: 'arrows' });`}</code></pre>

  <h2>In the frameworks</h2>
  <p>React <code>useMotionGesture('dismiss', &#123; onSwipe &#125;)</code>; Angular <code>udxMotionGesture="dismiss"</code> with the <code>(udxSwipe)</code>, <code>(udxDragEnd)</code> and <code>(udxReorder)</code> outputs; Svelte <code>&#123;&#64;attach motionGesture('dismiss', () =&gt; (&#123; onSwipe &#125;))&#125;</code>. The live examples swipe a notification away, and the list is rendered again with Restore.</p>
  <p>The item stays out of sight after it has been swiped, as the events describe. The examples do not remove it; the page can, once it is aria-hidden, as the <a href="/motion/demo#demo-swipe-list">demo</a> does.</p>
  <Code codes={{ react: reactSource, angular: angularSource, svelte: svelteSource }}>
    <MotionGestureReact slot="react" client:only="react" />
    <MotionGestureAngular slot="angular" client:load />
    <MotionGestureSvelte slot="svelte" client:only="svelte" />
  </Code>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code> on the element, a gesture's release is written at once, with no glide.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A gesture writes the <code>translate</code> of its element, and its <code>opacity</code> while a swipe flies out. An author's <code>translate</code> on that element is overwritten while it is bound.</li>
    <li><code>touch-action</code> is set when the gesture is bound, so a touch screen does not scroll the page instead of moving the element. It is given back on <code>destroy()</code>.</li>
    <li>A drag is bounded by the content box of its parent, measured when the pointer grabs the element and at each nudge of a key.</li>
    <li>A reorder moves an element among the siblings that carry the same gesture, under the same parent.</li>
    <li>A swipe that is not prevented stays in the DOM, with <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.</li>
    <li>A gesture's spec is validated in development only; its name is checked always.</li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    import { defineGesture } from '@udixio/motion/gesture';

    // The drag of the try-it section: it follows the pointer, and the arrow keys move it when it has focus.
    defineGesture('gesture-html-drag', { kind: 'drag', alternative: 'arrows' });
  </script>
</MotionPage>
